goinfer is a pure-Go LLM runtime. The SOURCE tree embeds no model weights, and
the plain `goinfer-chat-<os>-<arch>` binaries embed none either — you supply your
own open-weight checkpoint (safetensors, GGUF, GPTQ, or AWQ) at runtime, under
whatever license it carries.

TWO RELEASE ASSETS ARE THE EXCEPTION, and they are a redistribution of somebody
else's weights: `goinfer-chat-0.5b-*` and `goinfer-chat-1.5b-*` have a
Qwen2.5-Coder-Instruct GGUF compiled into them. See "Embedded model" below.
This file used to say the project "does not embed or distribute any model weights
itself", full stop, while twelve such binaries shipped with each release
(audit-2026-09-02 M-33).

